        "news_site": "ESA",
        "summary": "On 3 September 2026 at 15:49 CEST, the European Space Agency's\u00a0BepiColombo\u00a0Mission Control Team at the European Space Operations Centre (ESOC) received the signal they had been waiting for\u00a0\u2013\u00a0BepiColombo\u2019s\u00a0Mercury Transfer Module (MTM) successfully separated from the\u00a0spacecraft stack.\u00a0This landmark achievement for the ESA and\u00a0Japan\u00a0Aerospace Exploration\u00a0Agency\u00a0(JAXA)\u00a0mission marks the\u00a0first step of\u00a0BepiColombo's\u00a0long-awaited arrival at Mercury.\u00a0",
